// The whole suite runs once per entry, in order: round 1 on the canonical iBGP VXLAN fabric, round 2 on the eBGP VXLAN
// fabric. A switch belongs to one fabric, so the six VXLAN switches are re-homed into each round's fabric by the switch
// pre-flight (nd_ensure_switches.yaml; greenfield, ND erases and reloads them) and returned to the FIRST round's fabric
// after the last round. Round 1 runs the Consul files exactly as downloaded; every later round first re-targets them with
// `validate_nd_prerequisites.py render-round` (its fabric must be the registry's preserved fabric).
//   fabric    fabric the round runs on                          type      ND management.type that fabric must report
//   vpcType   nd_vpc_pair fabric_type used for the round's pair   label     shown in stage names and the Webex table
//   idSuffix  appended to the version id (output files, dynamic inventory, failure flag); empty keeps round 1 unchanged
